<div class="bt">Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim, Volume 2</div>
<div class="ht">Hilchos Birchos HaRe'iyah [Blessings of Seeing]<br>v'Sha'ar Brachos Pratiyos [and Other Specific Blessings]<br>Halachah 5, Part 2 (§§ 7–13)<br><span style="font-size:.95rem;font-weight:400">Based on <span class="lr">LM I, "Vayhi MiKetz — Zikaron"</span></span></div>

<div class="sn">§ 7 — <i>Baruch Chacham HaRazim</i>: The Blessing on Seeing Sixty Myriads of Israel</div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of the blessing: <span class="h">Baruch Chacham HaRazim</span> [Blessed is the Knower of Secrets] — said upon seeing sixty myriads of Israel. The more people gather, the more one can understand from them secrets and hints (= the memory mentioned above). <span class="h">Baruch Chacham HaRazim</span> — we bless Hashem for the secrets and hints He signals through them. As our Sages say: <span class="mx">"because no person's mind is the same as his fellow's."</span> See there in <span class="h">Brachos</span>, chapter <span class="h">HaRo'eh</span>. Ben Azzai saw a multitude on the Temple Mount and said: <span class="mx">"blessed is the Knower of Secrets, and blessed is He Who created all of these to serve me."</span> Ben Azzai certainly did not mean they serve him physically. Rather, his essential intention was that through them he could serve Hashem. Physically — they prepare food and clothing for him (<span class="mx">"how many labors Adam had to perform before he had bread to eat... yet I find all of these prepared before me"</span>), enabling him to engage in Hashem's service. Spiritually — he understands through them secrets and hints to draw close to Hashem, which is <span class="h">Baruch Chacham HaRazim</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 8 — Drawing Close to People of Truth Who Received from True <i>Tzadikim</i></div>

<div class="p">For this reason one must strive exceedingly to draw close to people of truth who received straight, true paths from true <span class="h">tzadikim</span>. The true <span class="h">tzadik</span> is the true victor — he merited defeating the evil inclination completely, with nothing of its filth remaining. He merited having no looking at this world at all — therefore the evil eye had no hold on him whatsoever. Therefore he merited wondrous memory, as understood from the story of "The Blind One" there (for based on this <span class="h">Torah</span>, one can somewhat understand what is written there — that the blind one, who had no looking at this world, had the most wondrous memory of all; see above and understand well). Through him one can merit the memory — constantly cleaving one's thought to the World to Come.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore, whenever there is a larger gathering at the true Rav, it is better to come then. The more Jews gather — especially people of truth coming for Heaven's sake to hear the word of Hashem — the more one can remind oneself of the purpose, understand the hints, and through this return to Hashem.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 9 — Every Small Movement for Heaven's Sake Is Eternally Precious</div>

<div class="p">Therefore one must know that every victory, however small, that a person achieves for Heaven's sake in truth — is exceedingly precious in Hashem's eyes. Every act and slight movement by which a person exerts himself to arrive at His will (strengthening himself to pray with intention and force, or shattering some trait, distancing himself from some craving, etc.) — how much more so when he overpowers to defeat the obstacles and draws himself close to a true Rav (upon which all his eternal vitality depends) — every single movement is exceedingly precious in Hashem's eyes. The instant one performs any act or movement for His will — he immediately wins a great amount of true, eternal victory. Only this is true victory — this victory will endure forever: <span class="mx">"no good will is ever lost."</span></div>

<div class="p">This is what Rabbainu <span class="h">zichrono livrachah</span> writes in many places regarding this. As he explains on: <span class="v">"when his waves rise, You still them"</span> — every time a person strengthens himself to lift himself toward Hashem through any movement whatsoever, <span class="mx">"this is His praise and His glory."</span> And as he explains regarding thoughts — it is exceedingly precious in His eyes when the pure creatures battle the impure creatures: when a person overpowers to defeat evil thoughts (as explained elsewhere). The instant he overpowers to defeat the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span>, he immediately merits holy victory — this slightest victory will remain forever and ever. Therefore, when one wants to travel to the true Rav — even though afterward a new, greater evil inclination overpowers (as explained elsewhere) — nevertheless, he has already won a great deal the instant he began traveling. Every movement of holy victory will remain forever: <span class="v">"You, Hashem, are exalted forever."</span></div>

<div class="sn">§ 10 — Thirty Days and Twelve Months: <i>Rosh Chodesh</i>, <i>Rosh HaShanah</i>, and <i>Yom HaZikaron</i></div>

<div class="p">Therefore the interval for blessing <span class="h">SheHechiyanu</span> upon seeing one's friend is thirty days (= one month); after twelve months, one blesses <span class="h">Mechayeh HaMaisim</span>. These blessings are to subdue the evil eye and merit the memory — reminding oneself through this renewed seeing of the World to Come.</div>

<div class="p">The measure is thirty days (= one month) because each month the memory is renewed further. Every thirty days (= one month), the tikun and filling of the moon's blemish is drawn — the tikun of the memory. The flaw of memory comes through the flaw of the moon (= the flaw of the evil eye from which the memory is damaged). Each month the moon is filled; we engage in its tikun through <span class="h">Rosh Chodesh</span> and <span class="h">Kiddush Levanah</span> [Sanctification of the Moon] — working to fill and repair it. Through this the memory is repaired: cleaving one's thought to the World to Come. Therefore on <span class="h">Rosh Chodesh</span> we say in <span class="h">Birchas Musaf</span>: <span class="v">"a remembrance for them all shall it be"</span> — the memory's tikun is then drawn. In <span class="h">Kiddush Levanah</span> we mention the reward of the World to Come: <span class="mx">"to the moon He said: it shall be renewed as a crown of glory for those borne from the womb, who are destined to be renewed like it."</span> The monthly renewal of the moon (= tikun and filling of its blemish) is the aspect of the renewal of Israel's souls for the World to Come. Therefore the memory is then renewed.</div>

<div class="p">In the days of the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span>, the sanctification of the new month was specifically through seeing [the new moon] — to subdue through this holy seeing the gaze of the evil eye that wants to flaw the memory of the World to Come (= the renewal of Israel's souls like the moon). Likewise the <span class="h">mitzvah</span> of <span class="h">Kiddush Levanah</span> depends on seeing — an exceedingly precious and important blessing, as our Sages say: <span class="mx">"if only..."</span> etc. Through the blessed seeing of the moon in its renewal (= <span class="h">Kiddush Levanah</span>), the evil eye is subdued and the memory of the World to Come is drawn.</div>

<div class="p">After a year, one blesses <span class="h">Mechayeh HaMaisim</span> on seeing a friend, because over the course of a year the memory needs greater renewal. This is <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> — which Hashem commanded us to observe at every yearly renewal, to renew the memory of the World to Come at each year's start. Therefore <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> is called <span class="h">Yom HaZikaron</span> [the Day of Remembrance] — the essential <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> is to renew the memory of the World to Come. <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> is the first of the Ten Days of <span class="h">Teshuvah</span>; then we must draw upon ourselves the awakening of <span class="h">teshuvah</span> — through the memory of the World to Come. Through remembering the World to Come where the great and awesome Day of Judgment awaits, one returns in <span class="h">teshuvah</span>. <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> is the Day of Judgment, corresponding to the Day of Judgment of the World to Come, as is known. Therefore we mention then the memory of the World to Come — that each person will need to give an accounting: <span class="v">"You remember the deeds of the world... You remember all that was done... there is no forgetfulness before Your Throne of Glory."</span> After twelve months, we bless <span class="h">Mechayeh HaMaisim</span> — explicitly mentioning the memory of the World to Come (= the Resurrection of the Dead, when the great and awesome Judgment of the World to Come will take place).</div>

<div class="sn">§ 11 — Sun and Moon: General and Particular Memory, and Why Israel Counts by the Moon</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> and <span class="h">Rosh Chodesh</span> (= the memory of the World to Come) are the aspects of memory in general and in particular — the light of the sun and the light of the moon. The essential light of the sun and moon illuminating the earth each day is the aspect of the illumination of <span class="h">da'as</span> — the memory: what Hashem in His goodness illuminates each day into every person's mind, that he should remember the World to Come. This is the essential purpose; only for this do we exist in the world. This is the essential renewal of Creation that Hashem renews every day: <span class="mx">"each day He opens the gates of the east, cleaves the windows of the firmament, brings forth the sun from its place and the moon from its dwelling, illuminating the entire world"</span> — all so people will see His wonders each day, remember Him, and cleave their thought to Him. This is the essential memory of the World to Come — when His G-dliness will be revealed further and <span class="v">"we shall see Him eye to eye"</span>: <span class="v">"for they shall all know Me."</span> One must draw this memory even now in this world: it is impossible to merit the World to Come without striving to remember it here — <span class="mx">"prepare yourself in the corridor."</span></div>

<div class="p">The essential light of the sun and moon is the light of Hashem illuminating through them: <span class="v">"Hashem is my light."</span> The essential hints Hashem sends to man every day — contracting Himself from the Infinite to the endless depths — are through the daily renewal of Creation. This is what our Sages say: <span class="v">"they do not gaze at the work of Hashem nor see the deeds of His hands"</span> — <span class="mx">"they did not praise the One Who forms light in the morning and brings on the evening in the evening."</span> This is the essential work and deed of Hashem that one must gaze at and see — understanding through them His greatness and the hints He sends every day.</div>

<div class="p">The light of the sun and moon are the aspects of general and particular memory. The sun's light (= the essential light) is the general memory of the World to Come: <span class="v">"the sun of righteousness shall shine for you who fear My Name"</span> (said of the World to Come); <span class="v">"those who love Him — like the sun going forth in its might."</span> The moon's light (= contracted light, for <span class="mx">"she has nothing of her own, only what she receives from the sun"</span>) is the particular memory: what Hashem contracts Himself through many contractions from the Infinite to the endless depths, reminding every person of his eternal purpose — the aspect of the moon's light (= contracted light).</div>

<div class="p">Hashem created them both equal: <span class="v">"the two great luminaries"</span> — wanting both to shine equally: that even in this world we should understand in particular through the hints the memory of the World to Come, perceiving Him as we will perceive Him in the World to Come itself. But through the moon's complaint (which came from the flaw of the evil eye), she was diminished and blemished — the essential flaw striking the particular aspect, as explained above.</div>

<div class="p">In general, everyone is forced to acknowledge the World to Come. But through flawing the particular, the general is also flawed — most forget completely or come to outright heresy, <span class="h">Rachmana litzlan</span>. Therefore the memory must be renewed each month (= the tikun of the moon's blemish): <span class="v">"a remembrance for them all."</span> The particular memory is repaired. Each year the general memory must be renewed entirely — <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> — the essential renewal of memory (hence: <span class="h">Yom HaZikaron</span>). <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> falls on <span class="h">Rosh Chodesh</span>: <span class="mx">"one remembrance ascends for both"</span> — the memory is renewed in both general and particular: <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> and <span class="h">Rosh Chodesh</span> together — sun and moon. Though the evil eye's essential hold is on the particular memory, since this flaw touches the general as well, the essential tikun on <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> renews the memory completely — general and particular. <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> and <span class="h">Rosh Chodesh</span> together: tikun of sun and moon — <span class="mx">"one remembrance ascends for both."</span> The essential tikun: drawing the general memory with such great light that it illuminates the particular in completeness — as explained above on <span class="v">"the sun shone for him,"</span> healing the thigh-wound (= particular memory's flaw). Through this the moon's blemish is repaired.</div>

<div class="p">The moon's blemish came through her saying: <span class="mx">"two kings cannot share one crown"</span> — she feared jealousy between them (= the flaw of the evil eye, from which all jealousies come). She asked Hashem for a tikun so the evil eye could not cause forgetfulness. Hashem answered: <span class="mx">"go and diminish yourself"</span> — since you fear the evil eye, you must diminish yourself; whoever cannot stand against the evil eye must flee from it (as explained in the above <span class="h">Torah</span>).</div>

<div class="p">The evil eye (= the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span>) will not be completely nullified until the end of time, so that free will exists. Therefore the moon's light had to be diminished — so the world would not see Israel's greatness (they who count by the moon, perceiving through <span class="h">emunah</span> = contraction), lest the nations attack them further (whoever cannot stand against the evil eye must flee).</div>

<div class="p">Therefore Israel counts by the moon — the days and years. The days are counted by the moon: this is the first of the month, that is the second, and after twenty-nine or thirty days — <span class="h">Rosh Chodesh</span>. Through this the memory is drawn: <span class="v">"a remembrance for them all"</span> — they remember that they are destined to be renewed like it for the World to Come. <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> too is counted by the moon — most years are three hundred and fifty-four days (twelve lunar months), sometimes adding a leap month to equalize moon and sun. The essential count of days and years is by the moon (= contraction, <span class="h">emunah</span>) — through which the essential memory comes. Since Israel counts their days and years by the moon, the evil eye certainly cannot overpower with its evil wisdom to cause forgetfulness of the World to Come, <span class="h">chas v'shalom</span>.</div>

<div class="p">Yet the nations too have a hold — the <span class="h">tekufos</span> [seasons] are counted by the sun: <span class="v">"they shall be for signs and seasons."</span> From there the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span> and the nations draw sustenance, counting by the sun — wanting to separate the sun from the moon, following only their wisdom, causing forgetfulness. Therefore the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span> has hold at each of the four seasons, as is known (people guard themselves at the time of the <span class="h">tekufah</span> — the evil eye having hold there, drawing from evil wisdoms: wisdom without <span class="h">emunah</span> — the nations counting by the sun alone). <span class="h">Tekufah</span> [season/cycle] — the aspect of: <span class="v">"they surrounded me like water all day, they encircled me together"</span> — the evil eye surrounding and encircling every day. Every day and year they overpower against us in many encirclements to cause forgetfulness of the true memory of the World to Come, <span class="h">chas v'shalom</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 12 — The Moon's Dialogue with Hashem: Diminishing, the <i>Tzadikim</i>, and the Root of <i>Teshuvah</i></div>

<div class="p">To explain the matter further, we must cite the saying of our Sages in the Gemara and explain it somewhat, as Hashem's good hand is upon us.</div>

<div class="p">The Gemara (<span class="h">Chulin</span> 60b): <span class="mx">"Rabbi Shimon ben Pazi raised a contradiction: it is written 'G-d made the two great luminaries,' yet it is written 'the small luminary.' The moon said before Hashem: 'Master of the World, can two kings share one crown?' He said to her: 'go and diminish yourself.' She said: 'because I said a proper thing before You, I should diminish myself?' He said: 'go and rule by day and by night.' She said: 'what use is a lamp in daylight?' He said: 'go — Israel shall count by you days and years.' She said: 'the day too — it is impossible they will not count seasons [<i>tekufos</i>] by it, as written: they shall be for signs and seasons and days and years.' 'Go — the <i>tzadikim</i> shall be called by your name: Yaakov the Small, Shmuel the Small, David the Small.' He saw that she was not consoled. Hashem said: 'bring an atonement for Me, that I diminished the moon.' This is what Raish Lakish said: 'why is the he-goat of <i>Rosh Chodesh</i> distinguished by 'for Hashem'? Hashem said: this he-goat shall be an atonement for Me for having diminished the moon.'"</span></div>

<div class="p">This passage is entirely wondrous, concealed, and exceedingly profound, as all the commentators struggled to find even a slender hint in it. It is known that this passage belongs to the deepest of the deep secrets of Torah — the matter of the moon's blemish, its filling and tikun, upon which the majority of Kabbalistic secrets depend. The crown of Torah rests upon all — I too shall answer my portion from the poverty of my meager understanding, through the fortified awesome greatness of the wondrous, profound foundations I received from our Master, our Teacher, our Rav — the holy and awesome one, <span class="h">the memory of the <i>tzadik</i> and holy one for blessing</span> — which, had our hearts been as open as the hearts of the first ones, we could expound the entire Torah, Written and Oral, based on one single teaching he revealed through his exceedingly lofty and concealed perception, without end or limit, as we heard from his holy mouth, <span class="h">zichrono livrachah</span>. Though we have not yet merited this due to the multitude of our sins, whatever we can strive and find in our holy Torah based on his holy, awesome foundations — it is a <span class="h">mitzvah</span> upon us to engage in this with all our might. Whatever we merit to innovate in Torah based on his holy foundations — from this shall flow springs of salvation for all: wondrous counsel, wondrous awakening, true <span class="h">mussar haskel</span>, to revive countless souls without end.</div>

<div class="p">Based on the above, a little can be explained. The moon said: <span class="mx">"two kings cannot share one crown"</span> — there would be jealousy between them, giving hold to the evil eye that causes forgetfulness. (The light of the eyes and the light of the sun and moon are one aspect — the essential seeing of the eyes is through the illuminating light of the sun and moon, through which light reaches the eye to see. We say: <span class="mx">"our eyes shine like the sun and moon."</span>) The flaw of the evil eye (= the flaw of the eyes) touches the sun and moon — primarily the moon, which had to diminish through it. She feared the evil eye and therefore complained: <span class="mx">"two kings cannot share one crown."</span></div>

<div class="p">Hashem answered: <span class="mx">"go and diminish yourself"</span> — since you fear the evil eye, you must diminish yourself (whoever cannot stand against the evil eye must flee, as explained in the above <span class="h">Torah</span>). The evil eye's essential attack causes forgetfulness of the particular memory (= the moon's light), since the sun and moon are the general and particular memory. She said: <span class="mx">"because I said a proper thing, I should diminish myself?"</span> — my intention was for good: I want Israel to remember the World to Come always with strong memory and great <span class="h">da'as</span> through <span class="h">emunah</span>; should I diminish myself for such a proper request?</div>

<div class="p">He said: <span class="mx">"go and rule by day and by night"</span> — it is impossible to completely fulfill your request (to nullify the evil eye entirely), for that is the world's sustenance (there must be free will and competition — everything was created for this). But what does it matter that you diminish and shrink yourself in their eyes? In truth, your dominion and victory are strong forever — in this world and the World to Come. Since their intention is truly for Heaven, to always remember the World to Come — they always win, however things unfold, even in the utmost smallness and lowliness. <span class="mx">"Go and rule by day and by night"</span> — hinting to the dominion of holy Israel in this world and the World to Come, as the Maharsha explains. Only the dominion and victory of holiness — which is eternal — is called dominion and victory; the opposite is not dominion at all. Though we are despised and lowly, pained and trampled, humbling ourselves greatly before them and forced to submit — this is our dominion and victory, for we always win since our intention is for Heaven. As our Sages say: <span class="mx">"one should always be flexible like a reed"</span> — even if bent to the ground a thousand times, it is strong at its root and all the winds in the world cannot uproot it. As Rabbainu <span class="h">zichrono livrachah</span> writes on: <span class="v">"Hashem has done great things with these — Hashem has done great things with us"</span> — even the nations will understand in the future that all their greatness and dominion was entirely our greatness and dominion (<span class="lr">LM I:21</span>).</div>

<div class="p">She said: <span class="mx">"a lamp in daylight — what use is it?"</span> — in this world (likened for them to day, their success being so great that it appears as if they alone shine, rule, and win) our victory and dominion are not discernible at all — like a lamp in daylight. Therefore, even though the truth is that the side of holiness always wins — most of the world does not see this, and many fall because they cannot bear the disgrace and lowliness. The evil eye overpowers greatly, appearing as if it wins, <span class="h">chas v'shalom</span> — casting much forgetfulness, making it difficult to guard the memory of the World to Come.</div>

<div class="p">He said: <span class="mx">"Israel shall count by you days and years"</span> — the aspect of <span class="v">"new every morning; great is Your faithfulness"</span>: Hashem renews Creation in His goodness every day — the contraction mentioned above, by which He contracts Himself every day from the Infinite to the endless depths, hinting to each person, reminding him of his eternal purpose. This is the essential daily renewal of Creation — <span class="v">"new every morning."</span> <span class="h">Limnoo</span> [they shall count] — like something counted that will not be lost. Israel counts by the moon — days and years. Through this they guard the days from forgetfulness (= loss). All the days are counted by the moon — this is the first of the month, that is the second — and at the end they make <span class="h">Rosh Chodesh</span>. Through this the memory is drawn: <span class="v">"a remembrance for them all"</span> — they remember they are destined to be renewed like it for the World to Come.</div>

<div class="p">She said: <span class="mx">"the day too — they must count seasons by it"</span> — the nations draw sustenance from there, counting by the sun (= wanting to separate sun from moon, following only their wisdom without <span class="h">emunah</span>, causing forgetfulness).</div>

<div class="p">He said: <span class="mx">"the <i>tzadikim</i> shall be called by your name — Yaakov the Small, Shmuel the Small, David the Small."</span> What you fear — that the evil eye overpowers so greatly that it would be impossible to stand against it in such smallness and lowliness — through the power of the great, true <span class="h">tzadikim</span> who won the war in the ultimate completeness, who humble and diminish themselves, descending to implant the memory of the World to Come in whoever wishes to hear the truth (even one of very lowly stature who did not stand firm in the war properly) — they revive and remind them through wondrous ways, contracting their intellect through many contractions until they can implant truth in their hearts. They are called "small" because they diminish themselves — the aspect of the "small luminary" (the moon), whose light was diminished from fear of the evil eye. The more one fears the evil eye, the more one must diminish the light, conceal it, contract it with wondrous wisdom so the lowly ones can receive it and the evil eye cannot confuse their minds and cause forgetfulness. This is the essential meaning of <span class="mx">"go and diminish yourself"</span> — specifically because of fear of the evil eye, one must diminish and contract the light further.</div>

<div class="p">These three <span class="h">tzadikim</span> — Yaakov, Shmuel, and David — are the root of the kingdom of <span class="h">Mashiach</span>, through which the evil eye is essentially subdued (as explained there). Yaakov is all of Israel, upon whom <span class="h">Mashiach</span>'s kingdom will rest — his bed was complete (twelve tribes of Hashem, corresponding to twelve months — all Israel with no admixture of the profane). He was the first to draw into the world the holiness of Israel exclusively (= the kingdom of <span class="h">Mashiach</span>). Shmuel anointed David, beginning to draw the kingdom of <span class="h">Mashiach</span> (= the kingdom of David). David himself is called <span class="h">Mashiach</span>: <span class="v">"the anointed one of the G-d of Yaakov."</span></div>

<div class="p"><span class="mx">"He saw she was not consoled"</span> — the exile lasts so long, who can bear it? The essential hope and assurance is to rely on the power of the true <span class="h">tzadikim</span> who truly humble themselves. But the evil eye attacks this very thing most fiercely, using all its might to distance people from such true <span class="h">tzadikim</span>.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="mx">"Hashem said: bring an atonement for Me"</span> — the he-goat of <span class="h">Rosh Chodesh</span>, through which the evil eye (= Esav, <span class="h">Ish Sa'ir</span> [the hairy man]) is essentially subdued. <span class="mx">"Bring an atonement for Me"</span> — with this He assured her: Israel will certainly remember Hashem and return to Him. Through the moon's arguments, until Hashem Himself, as it were, regretted and "repented" of having diminished her — from this the root of <span class="h">teshuvah</span> descends to the entire world, as Rabbainu writes (<span class="lr">LM I:10</span> and <span class="lr">LM II:1</span>): through this, <span class="h">teshuvah</span> flows to the entire world on <span class="h">Rosh Chodesh</span>. She is now assured: Israel will certainly remember the World to Come and return in <span class="h">teshuvah</span> — since she achieved that the root of <span class="h">teshuvah</span> (= Hashem Himself "regretting") was drawn through her arguments. From this root, thoughts of <span class="h">teshuvah</span> will certainly reach them until they truly return to Hashem.</div>

<div class="p">The moon prevailed with her arguments — she "defeated" Hashem until He regretted the diminishment and commanded Israel to bring an atonement for Him. From this come many hints and good hopes: we are assured He will not abandon us until we truly return. Since she achieved Hashem's "regret and return" — from this the root of <span class="h">teshuvah</span> descends. Since the moon prevailed in her arguments, this is a hint of salvation for us and all Israel who count by the moon — we have hope that we too will merit "defeating" Him in our <span class="h">tefilos</span> as the moon defeated Him in her arguments. Hashem desires this — that we overpower in <span class="h">tefilos</span>, conversations, and arguments with Him until we "defeat" Him: <span class="mx">"<i>LaMenatzeach</i>... sing to Him Whom one defeats and He rejoices."</span> Hashem is the true Victor: <span class="v">"the Eternal One of Israel does not lie"</span> — He despises false victory. His essential victory is when we defeat Him, achieving that He returns us to Himself. For this is what He desires: <span class="v">"call upon Me in the day of trouble; I shall deliver you, and you shall honor Me."</span></div>

<div class="p">Also, through Hashem asking Israel to atone for Him (<span class="mx">"bring an atonement for Me"</span>), He informed them that His atonement, as it were, depends on them — He "cannot" repair the moon's diminishment (which caused the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span>'s hold and the length of exile) except through Israel who will atone for Him: <span class="mx">"a prisoner cannot free himself from prison."</span></div>

<div class="p">This is: <span class="v">"a hand upon the throne of Y-H"</span> — the Name is not complete; <span class="v">"Hashem swore by His right hand... that He will not turn back the right hand"</span> (as brought in the holy Zohar). In all of this He informs us that He Himself is always with us in all troubles and exiles, not leaving until we atone for Him (= return in <span class="h">teshuvah</span>): <span class="mx">"this matter depends only on <i>teshuvah</i>, and His redemption — which is <i>teshuvah</i> — depends on their hands."</span> Therefore ultimately we must certainly return to Him — since His own atonement depends on this, and He will certainly finish His task, for He is the Victor over all victors. This itself is the assurance He gave the Congregation of Israel: that He would be with them in exile — through which they would certainly not be lost there, as explained in our Sages' words many times. This is <span class="mx">"bring an atonement for Me"</span> — through which we are assured we will certainly return to Him truly. The essential atonement is <span class="h">teshuvah</span>; since His atonement depends on our <span class="h">teshuvah</span> — we will certainly return, for He will certainly prevail.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 13 — <i>Rosh Chodesh</i>: The He-Goat, Memory, and Salvation from the Enemy</div>

<div class="p">On <span class="h">Rosh Chodesh</span> — tikun of the moon's blemish (= subduing the evil eye), through which memory is drawn. <span class="v">"A remembrance for them all shall it be, and salvation of their souls from the hand of the enemy"</span> — the evil eye is the essential enemy, subdued on <span class="h">Rosh Chodesh</span>, through which memory is drawn. All this is repaired through the he-goat of <span class="h">Rosh Chodesh</span> — the essential tikun and filling of the moon's blemish (= tikun of memory): <span class="mx">"bring an atonement for Me."</span></div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"Beginnings of months You gave to Your people... and he-goats of sin-offerings to atone for them — a remembrance for them all shall it be, and salvation of their souls from the hand of the enemy."</span> The essential tikun of memory and subduing of the evil eye — <span class="v">"a remembrance for them all... salvation of their souls from the hand of the enemy"</span> — is accomplished through the sin-offering he-goats of <span class="h">Rosh Chodesh</span>. It all connects and joins beautifully.</div>

